.TH RM 1
.SH NAME
rm \- remove files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rm
.RB [ \-f ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rm
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It removes each
.I file
(a name: the file itself goes when its last link does), and stops at the
first one it cannot remove. In
.B /tmp
(sticky) only a file's owner may remove it. Directories are removed with
.BR rmdir (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
A file that does not exist is not an error.
.B \-f
must come first.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on the first failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR ln (1),
.BR snap (1),
.BR sh (1)
